00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.529
The David Pakman Show subreddit is approaching
a huge milestone.

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:07.120
Twenty thousand subscribers.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:12.490
You can find it at David Pakman dot com slash
rbd d-i t.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:14.690
Couple interesting posts from this morning.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.900
Lime guy asked how many of you are friends
with trombonists?

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.760
Do you think politics matters with friends?

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.890
This is something I've never come to a conclusion
on though.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:28.090
I find people who believe really dumb crap
can be annoying to me like Trump apologists.

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:35.899
You know, for me, the conflicts with conservative
acquaintances and friends are are rarely about

00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:41.559
politics themselves, but it's about something
indirectly related to their worldview.

00:00:41.559 --> 00:00:48.519
So like we rarely argue about electoral politics
or abortion or stuff like that.

00:00:48.519 --> 00:00:54.039
But what gets irritating and tends to cause
conflict is that their political views are

00:00:54.039 --> 00:00:59.420
linked to a generally bizarre world view,
which might include, you know, aggressive

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:05.329
skepticism of science or conspiratorial thinking
about uncontroversial institutions or whatever

00:01:05.329 --> 00:01:06.329
the case may be.

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:11.860
So in my experience, the difficulty with acquaintances,
colleagues, friends that whose politics are

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:20.070
different is not so much about the politics
of electoral decisions, so to speak, but more

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:24.119
just that, like their politics are just part
of a worldview.

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:30.130
That to me is difficult to be around, and
very often I end up sort of opting out.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:33.570
I'm talking about pretty radical people here,
like some kind of moderate centrist where

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.729
we disagree on on fiscal policy.

00:01:35.729 --> 00:01:39.460
It's not really a huge deal, but but that's
typically what happens.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:44.560
The arguments aren't actually about Social
Security or abortion or gay marriage or whatever

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:45.649
the case may be.

00:01:45.649 --> 00:01:53.600
I also posted by Reflex Point is a very interesting
section of Sam Harris interviewing Andrew

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:55.280
Yang on two issues.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.969
Joe Biden's cognitive state, as well as Tara
Reid.

00:01:58.969 --> 00:02:01.000
I encourage people to check this out.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.840
I tend to have the same perspective as Andrew
Yang.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:09.251
Here he explains when it comes to Joe Biden's
cognitive state that, listen, he's 78 and

00:02:09.251 --> 00:02:15.790
thus he is a different person cognitively
to some degree, as he was when he debated

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:19.260
Paul Ryan eight almost nine years ago.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:25.540
But that Andrew Yang has spent time with him
and Joe Biden is cognitively OK and that all

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.030
of the stuff that we're seeing is relatively
overblown.

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:33.950
That goes with what I'm seeing from the mental
health experts that I talked to and the neurologists

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:35.140
that I've spoken to.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:40.280
I would not doubt for a second that Joe Biden
is not slowed down compared to who he was

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:43.140
nine, 12, 15, 20 years ago.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.310
He's nearly 80 years old.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:46.640
And this is something that happens.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:49.600
But I concur with Andrew Yang on that.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:56.950
Andrew Yang also says that he does not think
that the terror Reid story is going to explode

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:01.700
and be the prevailing narrative over the next
few months with Joe Biden.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:04.570
And I also agree with that and I've explained
why earlier this week.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:06.820
So check out that video if you haven't seen
it.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:09.200
